1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560
What an intriguing group of individuals you are.
你们真是一群有意思的人。

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:15,600
To a psychologist I've had the opportunity over the last couple of days of listening in on some of your conversations and watching you interact with each other.
对一位心理学家来说，过去几天我有机会旁听你们的一些谈话，也观察你们彼此互动。

3
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:28,550
And I think it's fair to say already that there are 47 people in this audience at this moment displaying psychological symptoms.
而且我觉得，现在已经可以说，这一刻在场有四十七个人正在表现出某些心理症状。

4
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:36,240
I would like to discuss today and I thought you might like to know who you are.
这些是我今天想讨论的内容，我想你们也许会想知道，我说的是谁。

5
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:48,880
But instead of pointing at you which would be gratuitous and intrusive I thought I would tell you a few facts and stories in which you may catch a glimpse of yourself.
不过，指着你们说既没有必要，也很冒犯，所以我想讲几个事实和故事，你们也许能从中看到自己的一点影子。

6
00:00:48,880 --> 00:01:02,240
I'm in the field of research known as personality psychology which is part of a larger personality science which spans the full spectrum from neurons to narratives.
我的研究领域叫人格心理学，它属于更广泛的人格科学，研究范围从神经元一直延伸到人生叙事。

7
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:15,920
And what we try to do in our own way is to make sense of how each of us each of you is in certain respects like all other people.
我们各自以自己的方式，试着理解：我们每个人、你们每个人，在某些方面都像所有其他人。

8
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,520
Like some other people and like no other person.
在另一些方面像某些人，又有些方面不像任何其他人。

9
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:34,800
Now already you may be saying of yourself I'm not intriguing I am the 46 th most boring person in the western hemisphere.
此刻你可能已经在心里说：我并不有趣，我可是整个西半球第四十六无聊的人。

10
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:45,359
Or you may say of yourself I am intriguing even if I am regarded by most people as a great thundering twit.
或者你会说：我很有意思，即使大多数人把我当成一个十足的大傻瓜。

11
00:01:45,359 --> 00:01:56,080
But it is your self diagnosed boringness and your inherent twittiness that makes me as a psychologist really fascinated by you.
但恰恰是你自认的无聊，以及你自带的那点傻气，让我这个心理学家对你特别好奇。

12
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:59,199
So let me explain why this is so.
所以，让我解释一下为什么会这样。

13
00:01:59,199 --> 00:02:04,800
One of the most influential approaches in personality science is known as trait psychology.
人格科学中一种很有影响力的方法，叫作特质心理学。

14
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:18,240
And it aligns you along five dimensions which are normally distributed that describe universally um held aspects of difference between people.
它把你放在五个呈正态分布的维度上，这些维度描述了人们普遍存在的差异，嗯，就是那些共有的差异方面。

15
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:26,640
Uh they spell out the acronym ocean so o stands for open to experience versus those who are more closed.
呃，它们组成缩写 OCEAN。O 代表乐于接受新体验，对应的是更封闭的人。

16
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:33,520
C stands for conscientiousness in contrast to those with a more lackadaisical approach to life.
C 代表尽责性，对应的是对生活比较散漫的态度。

17
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:38,160
E extraversion in contrast to more introverted people.
E 是外向性，与更内向的人相对。

18
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:44,640
A agreeable individuals in contrast to those decidedly not agreeable.
A 是随和友善的人，与明显不那么随和的人相对。

19
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:51,199
And an neurotic individuals in contrast to those who are more stable.
还有神经质倾向较高的人，与情绪更稳定的人相对。

20
00:02:51,199 --> 00:02:57,680
All of these dimensions have implications for our well being for how our life goes.
所有这些维度，都关系到我们的福祉，也关系到我们生活过得怎样。

21
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:05,680
And so we know that for example openness and conscientiousness are very good predictors of life success.
所以我们知道，例如，开放性和尽责性都是人生成功的良好预测因素。

22
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:12,880
But the open people achieve that success through being audacious and occasionally odd.
但开放性高的人，靠大胆、偶尔有点古怪来取得这种成功。

23
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:22,640
The conscientious people achieve it through sticking to deadlines to persevering as well as having some passion.
尽责的人则靠守住截止时间、坚持下去，以及保持一些热情来取得成功。

24
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:29,839
Extroversion and agreeableness are both conducive to working well with people.
外向性和宜人性，都有助于与人合作。

25
00:03:29,839 --> 00:03:39,199
Extroverts for example I find intriguing with my classes I sometimes give them a basic fact that might be revealing with respect to their personality.
比如，我觉得外向的人很有意思。我有时会告诉班上的学生一个基本事实，它也许能透露他们的人格特点。

26
00:03:39,199 --> 00:03:49,520
I tell them that it is virtually impossible for adults to lick the outside of their own elbow.
我告诉他们，成年人几乎不可能舔到自己手肘的外侧。

27
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:56,720
Did you know that already some of you have tried to lick the outside of your own elbow.
你们知道这个吗？已经有人试着去舔自己的手肘外侧了。

28
00:03:56,720 --> 00:04:06,160
But extroverts amongst you are probably those who have not only tried but they have successfully licked the elbow of the person sitting next to them.
不过，你们当中外向的人，大概不但试了，还成功舔到了坐在旁边那个人的手肘。

29
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:08,079
Those are the extroverts.
那些就是外向的人。
